                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "titanium-diaphragm":</h3><p>Most condenser microphones have diaphragms of lightweight, thin polyester (e.g. Mylar) film metallized with a thin coating of gold. A small percentage of condenser mics use alternative diaphragm materials, such as aluminum. </p><p>Microphones tagged <b>titanium-diaphragm</b> employ titanium diaphragms. Titanium diaphragms are lighter weight, stronger, and more resistant to temperature changes or moisture, than are gold-coated polyester-film diaphragms.</p>
